Bound every byte the RICE_1 decoders read by the compressed tile buffer.

fits_rdecomp, fits_rdecomp_short and fits_rdecomp_byte checked for the end
of the input only after each block of nblock pixels, so a corrupt tile (a
tile descriptor that shortens the stream, flipped data bytes, or a hostile
ZVAL1 block size) made them read past the end of the heap buffer before
reporting 'hit end of compressed byte stream'. Every byte fetch now checks
the end first; the short and byte decoders also refuse an input too short
for the leading raw pixel, as the int decoder already did.

--- a/ricecomp.c
+++ b/ricecomp.c
@@ -862,6 +862,25 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 */
 
+/* Fetch the next byte of the compressed stream, or fail when the stream is
+   exhausted.  The decoders used to check for the end of the input only
+   after each block of nblock pixels, so a corrupt tile (or a hostile
+   ZVAL1 block size) made them read past the end of the buffer. */
+#define RDECOMP_GET(dst) do { \
+    if (c >= cend) { \
+        ffpmsg("decompression error: hit end of compressed byte stream"); \
+        return 1; \
+    } \
+    (dst) = *c++; \
+} while (0)
+#define RDECOMP_SHIFT_IN(dst) do { \
+    if (c >= cend) { \
+        ffpmsg("decompression error: hit end of compressed byte stream"); \
+        return 1; \
+    } \
+    (dst) = ((dst)<<8) | (*c++); \
+} while (0)
+
 /*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 /* this routine used to be called 'rdecomp'  (WDP)  */
 
